messages:
When the renderer sends a bad DPR, we call mojo::ReportBadMessage() and return without ever calling callback. The CaptureScreenshotCallback destructor does nothing (DomainDispatcher::Callback::~Callback() = default), so the Page.captureScreenshot command never gets an answer. The DevTools/WebDriver client just hangs until it times out.

Please also send a failure before returning, for example:

```
mojo::ReportBadMessage("Invalid device pixel ratio for screenshot.");
callback->sendFailure(Response::ServerError("Unable to determine viewport for screenshot."));
return;
```

Please also add a test that checks the client gets an error in this case.

optional nit: Clarify why all `seq_N` signatures must share the same fixed `max_options` (e.g. ai suggests):

```suggestion
      // Every seq_N signature must share the same fixed max_options capacity,
      // since LayaQueryAdapter builds marker tensors before seq_N is chosen.
```
